== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [Which of these is a disaccharide?], [glucose], [lactose], [fructose], [cellulose])

#mcq(2, [A gas that turns acidified potassium dichromate(VI) green is], [carbon dioxide], [hydrogen], [oxygen], [sulphur(IV) oxide])

#mcq(3, [Which statement about the alkanes is true?], [They burn in oxygen], [They decolourise bromine water], [They are oxidized by acidified potassium manganate(VII)], [They react with sodium hydroxide])

#mcq(4, [The product formed when ethene reacts with bromine in tetrachloromethane is], [bromoethane], [ethane], [1,2-dibromoethane], [bromoethene])

#mcq(5, [The oxidation of ethanol in the body is catalysed by], [zymase in the blood], [amylase in the saliva], [alcohol dehydrogenase in the liver], [pepsin in the stomach])

#mcq(6, [The general formula of an ester made from a monocarboxylic acid and a monoalcohol is], [CₙH₂ₙ₊₂O], [CₙH₂ₙ₋₂O₂], [CₙH₂ₙ₊₁O], [CₙH₂ₙO₂])

#mcq(7, [Kwashiorkor is a deficiency disease caused by a lack of], [protein], [vitamin C], [iron], [carbohydrate])

#mcq(8, [The test for a chloride in solution uses], [barium chloride and acid], [silver nitrate acidified with nitric acid], [sodium hydroxide], [limewater])

#mcq(9, [Which of these fractions has the highest boiling point?], [petrol], [lubricating oil], [diesel], [kerosene])

#mcq(10, [The main product when ethene is oxidised by cold dilute acidified permanganate is], [ethanoic acid], [carbon dioxide], [ethane-1,2-diol], [ethanol])

#mcq(11, [The enzyme in yeast that catalyses fermentation is], [amylase], [urease], [lipase], [zymase])

#mcq(12, [The soap molecule is said to be amphiphilic because it has], [a hydrophilic head and a hydrophobic tail], [two ionic ends], [a positive and a negative charge on the same atom], [no charge])

#mcq(13, [The test for a reducing sugar uses], [iodine solution, at room temperature], [Biuret reagent], [Benedict's solution, boiled], [bromine water])

#mcq(14, [A compound melts over the range 118–124 °C. This suggests that it is], [pure], [a gas], [a metal], [impure])

#mcq(15, [Which of these is the best evidence that a sample of crude oil is a mixture?], [it has no sharp boiling point], [it is dark in colour], [it floats on water], [it burns])

#mcq(16, [The polymer of styrene is used in], [non-stick surfaces], [packaging and insulation foam], [drain pipes], [car tyres])

#mcq(17, [Which of these compounds would react with both sodium carbonate and ethanol?], [ethanal], [ethanoic acid], [ethane], [ethyl ethanoate])

#mcq(18, [The mass of soap, C₁₇H₃₅COONa, that can be made from 0.100 mol of a triglyceride is], [30.6 g], [61.2 g], [91.8 g], [9.18 g])

#mcq(19, [In the body, excess glucose is stored as], [glycogen], [cellulose], [protein], [fat only])

#mcq(20, [The concentration of a solution in mol dm⁻³ is calculated as], [moles ÷ volume in cm³], [mass ÷ volume], [moles × volume], [moles ÷ volume in dm³])

#mcq(21, [Which procedure would separate a mixture of two liquid alkanes with boiling points of 69 °C and 98 °C?], [filtration], [fractional distillation], [crystallisation], [chromatography])

#mcq(22, [Which reagent converts ethyne into ethane?], [hydrogen over nickel], [bromine water], [sodium hydroxide], [acidified dichromate])

#mcq(23, [Which statement about ethanol and water is correct?], [They form two layers], [Ethanol floats on water and does not mix], [Ethanol reacts with water to give ethanoic acid], [They mix in all proportions])

#mcq(24, [Which statement about the hydrolysis of an ester is correct?], [It produces only water], [It cannot be catalysed], [It is the reverse of esterification], [It produces a ketone])

#mcq(25, [Which of these is a non-reducing sugar?], [maltose], [sucrose], [lactose], [glucose])

#mcq(26, [A flame test gives an apple-green colour. The metal is], [calcium], [copper], [barium], [lithium])

#mcq(27, [Which pair are isomers?], [methane and ethane], [ethanol and ethanoic acid], [ethene and ethyne], [butane and 2-methylpropane])

#mcq(28, [The IUPAC name of CH₃CH=CHCH₃ is], [but-2-ene], [but-1-ene], [2-methylpropene], [butane])

#mcq(29, [Which of these is a use of ethanoic acid?], [as a preservative and flavouring in vinegar], [as a fuel in cars], [as a fertiliser], [as a refrigerant])

#mcq(30, [The main product of the reaction between ethanoic acid and methanol is], [ethyl methanoate], [methanoic acid], [methanol], [methyl ethanoate])

#mcq(31, [The chemical name for table sugar is], [glucose], [sucrose], [fructose], [maltose])

#mcq(32, [25.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol dm⁻³ sodium hydroxide is neutralised by 20.0 cm³ of hydrochloric acid. The acid concentration is], [0.080 mol dm⁻³], [0.200 mol dm⁻³], [0.125 mol dm⁻³], [0.500 mol dm⁻³])

#mcq(33, [The fraction with the lowest boiling range is], [naphtha], [kerosene], [refinery gas], [lubricating oil])

#mcq(34, [Which process would produce ethene from ethanol?], [warming with sodium], [heating with concentrated sulphuric acid at 170 °C], [oxidising with acidified dichromate], [reacting with bromine water])

#mcq(35, [Which of these alcohols is used as an antifreeze?], [ethane-1,2-diol], [methanol], [ethanol], [propane-1,2,3-triol (glycerol)])

#mcq(36, [Which of these is a thermosetting plastic?], [poly(ethene)], [poly(propene)], [polystyrene], [urea–methanal resin])

#mcq(37, [Which test would you use to show that a sample contains both starch and a reducing sugar?], [iodine, then Benedict's], [Biuret, then iodine], [Benedict's only], [the emulsion test])

#mcq(38, [Which cation gives no precipitate with sodium hydroxide but gives a brick-red flame?], [Na⁺], [K⁺], [Ca²⁺], [Cu²⁺])

#mcq(39, [A student heats a mixture of kerosene and water in a separating funnel. The kerosene is found], [in the lower layer], [in the upper layer], [dissolved in the water], [at the bottom with the water])

#mcq(40, [The mass of poly(ethene) that can be made from 140 g of ethene at 100 % conversion is], [28 g], [70 g], [280 g], [140 g])

